<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94755" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκευωρ-έομαι</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκευωρησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					45.47
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκευώρημαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					32.9
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>:—
				Act.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκευωρέω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.569
				</span></i>
			; and pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκευώρημαι</span> in pass. sense, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				45.5
			</span></i>:—prop. <i>look after the baggage</i> or
				<i>utensils</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκεύη</span>), but only
			found in general sense, <i>inspect, examine thoroughly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς τάφους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					16.1.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τὴν Πομπηΐου οἰκίαν</span>
			<i>ransack</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				51
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cam.</u>
				32
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.587f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>contrive, manage, fabricate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				32.9
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				45.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				46.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Oen.
				24
			</span></i>; with a sense of <i>fraud</i> or <i>intrigue</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀν Πελοποννήσῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					9.17
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὑποκρίσεις</span>
			<i>contrive</i> dramatic effects, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.711e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> intr.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. περὶ τὰς νεοττιάς</span>
			<i>to be busy</i> about them, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				619a24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>act knavishly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					17.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> abs.,
				<i>plagiarize</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.61
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
